@* Table's Selection page, moved from its Overview: checkboxes in a form, then bulk actions. *@

<Heading Level="2">Selecting rows</Heading>
<TextBlock>Row selection adds a checkbox to each row, so the user can pick rows to act on. Set <Code>SelectionMode="SelectionMode.Multiple"</Code> and give the table an <Code>ItemKey</Code>. For a radio button on each row instead, set <Code>SelectionMode.Single</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="table-select-rows" />
<TextBlock>In a form, the checked rows post their keys, so selection works with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>. On static pages, read the keys as a <Code>Selection</Code> with <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm(Name = "selected")]</Code>. On interactive pages, bind it with <Code>@@bind-Selection</Code>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>To get the selected items from a query, call the selection's <Code>Apply</Code>. The totals under this example come from the columns' <Code>FooterText</Code>; see <Anchor Href="docs/components/table#totals-row">Totals row</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Bulk actions</Heading>
<TextBlock>Bulk actions are buttons that act on every selected row at once. To show them in a bar above the rows, set <Code>SelectionActions</Code>. The bar is always there, so selecting a row doesn't move the rows.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="table-bulk-actions" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>The buttons are disabled until a row is selected. A link can't be disabled, so a link in the bar stays active.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>While rows are selected, the footer shows how many, with a Clear selection button.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>The selection stays as the user pages, sorts and filters.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Shift-clicking a checkbox selects or clears every row from the last one clicked.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With JavaScript off, only the rows checked on the current page post.</ListItem>
</List>
<TextBlock>The header checkbox selects the rows on the current page. To make it select every row the filters match, on any page, set <Code>SelectAllMode="SelectAllMode.All"</Code>. Those rows aren't loaded, so call <Code>Apply</Code> to find them; changing the filter clears this selection.</TextBlock>
